      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, which is almost four times the usual maximum adult dose of 4 g/day. Many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A dose like that risks acute liver failure and could be fatal, even with normal liver function. A single 5 g dose is already in the range where toxicity is a concern for a 70 kg patient.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg** PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 5,000 mg TID is what you intend, for example for a protocol I don't know about, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy before it's entered."
      }
     ],
