      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 15 g/day, acetaminophen carries a serious risk of fatal liver injury. I don't know of any clinical rationale that supports it. Your seniority doesn't change the pharmacology, and entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a dose within the safe range, such as 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum). Tell me which one.\n- Help you work out a different plan if the goal is stronger analgesia or fever control. That would mean adding or changing agents, not raising the acetaminophen dose.\n- If you think there's a legitimate reason for this dose, take it to pharmacy or your P&T process. Those routes can review it and put it through with the right safeguards.\n\nIf the \"5000\" was a typo, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
